  <num>KL-CY-2025-023</num>
  <heading>Kiowa Criminal Code</heading>
  <meta>
    <effective>2025-10-21</effective>
    <history>
      <adopted>2025-10-11</adopted>
    </history>
    <citations>
      <citation type="res" url="./adopted/KL-CY-2025-023.pdf">Kiowa Tribe Res. No. KL-CY-2025-023</citation>
    </citations>
  </meta>
  <recitals>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>WHEREAS,</conjunction>
      <text> the Kiowa Tribe is a federally recognized Indian Tribe with a Constitution approved by the Secretary of the Interior; and,</text>
    </recital>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>WHEREAS,</conjunction>
      <text> the Legislature, is vested with the authority to pass laws and resolutions pursuant to <cite doc="Constitution of the Kiowa Tribe">Article VI, Section 6 (a) of the Constitution of the Kiowa Tribe</cite>; and,</text>
    </recital>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>WHEREAS,</conjunction>
      <text> the Legislature, is authorized under the Kiowa Constitution and is empowered to promulgate and enforce codes and laws, to protect Kiowa Tribal Citizens; and,</text>
    </recital>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>WHEREAS,</conjunction>
      <text> this Kiowa Criminal Code is intended to replace the previous criminal codes of the Kiowa Tribe; and,</text>
    </recital>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>WHEREAS,</conjunction>
      <text> this Kiowa Criminal Code is further intended to adopt certain provisions related to Special Tribal Criminal Jurisdiction as established in the United States' Violence Against Women Act, see e.g. 25 U.S.C. 1304.</text>
    </recital>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>NOW, THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED,</conjunction>
      <text> the Kiowa Tribe Legislature, having been delegated certain authorities under the Kiowa Constitution, the governing body of the Kiowa Tribe, does hereby adopt the attached "Kiowa Criminal Code."</text>
    </recital>
    <recital>
      <conjunction>BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED,</conjunction>
      <text> that any laws substantially similar to the attached Kiowa Criminal Code, such as the Kiowa Code of 2017 and the updated version of the Kiowa Code of 2017 included in the Kiowa Tribe Code of Laws (but not the Kiowa Tribe Peacekeeping Act), are hereby repealed.</text>
    </recital>
  </recitals>
